Kestrel Voidwing <EXECUTOR> — W2.5e plan addendum: guard::submit_pty returns RecipientStored when it refuses to type because its existing caller is W2.4 messaging, which already stored the body. A direct MCP input refusal has no stored recipient text (the control audit stores only args_digest). I will map that case to rejected/not submitted with the guard reason and no delivery claim, not falsely advertise recipient persistence. NativeWritten remains fully PTY-written only; NativeUnknown stays unknown/no replay. This changes no existing messaging behavior.
